# security/shadow_ai/known_ai_allowlist.conf -- Shadow AI Monitor's
# own allowlist of AI processes/ports/domains THIS deployment has
# explicitly reviewed and approved. Anything shadow_ai_monitor.sh's
# scan matches against shadow_ai_signatures.conf but does NOT also
# match here is reported as unexpected ("Shadow AI").
#
# format: TYPE|PATTERN|LABEL
#   TYPE    - process | port | domain (same meaning as
#             shadow_ai_signatures.conf's own TYPE column)
#   PATTERN - matched the same way the corresponding signature type is
#             matched (substring for process/domain, exact number for
#             port)
#   LABEL   - free-form description (documentation only)
# lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# This is an example/template (same Public/Private Security Boundary
# convention as security/egress_allowlist.conf.example): copy it to
# security/shadow_ai/known_ai_allowlist.conf and fill in what THIS
# deployment has actually reviewed and approved. The real file is
# gitignored. Missing entirely is NOT fail-closed here the way
# egress_allowlist.conf is for egress_check() -- shadow_ai_monitor.sh
# is a pure detector with no gating authority over anything (see its
# own header), so an empty/missing allowlist just means "nothing is
# pre-approved yet," and every AI signature match is reported as
# unexpected until reviewed and added here.
process|claude|Claude Code CLI -- this deployment's own primary AI tool
domain|api.anthropic.com|Anthropic API -- this deployment's own reviewed AI vendor (see security/egress_allowlist.conf's Takomachi gateway entry)
